      398.07,
      125.73
    ],
    "text": "COLLECTIVE AGREEMENT No. 19 OF 2024",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      142.66,
      542.26,
      167.73
    ],
    "text": "This Collective Agreement made this Fourteenth Day of December Two Thousand and Twenty Three to take e\ufb00 ect from the First day of July Two Thousand and Twenty Three pursuant to the Industrial Disputes Act between.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      184.66,
      542.26,
      237.73
    ],
    "text": "Dipped Products PLC (PQ60), having its registered o\ufb03 ce at 400, Deans Road, Colombo 10 (hereinafter referred to as the \"Employer') of the One Part and the Inter Company Employees' Union a registered Trade Union having its o\ufb03 ce at 10, Council Lane, Dehiwala (hereinafter referred to as the 'Union') of the Second Part Witnesseth and it is hereby agreed between the parties as follows:",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      254.66,
      542.21,
      279.73
    ],
    "text": "TITLE : This Agreement shall be known and referred to as the DIPPED PRODUCTS PLC PLANT 2 (FORMERLY NEOPREX) OPERATIONS ASSISTANTS' COLLECTIVE AGREEMENT OF 2023",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      232.15,
      296.66,
      355.52,
      307.73
    ],
    "text": "COLLECTIVE AGREEMENT",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      324.66,
      542.28,
      377.73
    ],
    "text": "This Agreement is entered into between DIPPED PRODUCTS PLC, a duly incorporated Company bearing Registration No. PQ60 having its registered o\ufb03 ce at 400, Deans Road, Colombo 10, Sri Lanka (hereinafter referred to as the \"Employer\"). and the Inter Company Employees' Union, a duly registered Trade Union having its registered o\ufb03 ce at No. 10, Council Lane. Dehiwala (hereinafter referred to as the \"Union\")",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      394.66,
      542.28,
      433.73
    ],
    "text": "WHEREAS the Union made certain demands of the Employer for the revision of terms and conditions of employment of their members employed by the Employer at Dipped Products Plant 2 (formerly known as Neoprex) and the parties after negotiations arrived at the following Agreement.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      450.66,
      542.26,
      489.73
    ],
    "text": "1. Parties Covered And Bound.\u2013 The terms of this Collective Agreement shall cover and bind the Employer, the Union and members of the Union employed on permanent monthly contracts by the Employer at Dipped Products Plant 2 (formerly known as Neoprex) as Operations Assistants in the Manual/Operative grades.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.75,
      506.66,
      542.28,
      587.73
    ],
    "text": "2. Duration.\u2013 This Agreement shall take e\ufb00 ect from the First day of July Two Thousand and Twenty Three and shall, unless otherwise terminated by either party giving two months'. written notice to the other, continue to remain in force provided, however, that neither party shall give such notice prior to the Thirtieth day of April Two Thousand and Twenty Six and the Agreement shall not stand terminated prior to the Thirtieth day of June Two Thousand and Twenty Six. Further, it is agreed by and between parties that neither shall attempt to vary or alter the terms of this Agreement during the pendency of same other than by mutual agreement.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.74,
      604.66,
      542.27,
      643.73
    ],
    "text": "3. Salaries.\u2013 The salary scales applicable to Employees covered and bound by this Agreement and hereinafter referred to as Employees, with e\ufb00 ect from First day of July Two Thousand and Twenty Three shall be as set out in Schedule I hereto.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.74,
      660.66,
      529.0,
      699.73
    ],
    "text": "3.1 To ascertain the monthly salary payable to an Employee with e\ufb00 ect from First day of July Two Thousand and Twenty Three a sum of Rs.7,000/- will be added to the salary paid to such employees as at the Thirtieth day of June Two Thousand and Twenty Three.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      47.74,
      716.66,
      528.35,
      755.73
    ],
    "text": "3.2 With e\ufb00 ect from the First day of July Two Thousand and Twenty Four, the monthly salaries of employees will be revised and a sum of Rs.6,000/- will be added to the salary paid to such employees as at the Thirtieth day of June Two Thousand and Twenty Four.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      107.59,
      85.96,
      495.61,
      97.48
    ],
    "text": "I fldgi: (I) fPoh \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2025'03'03",
    "fonts": [
      "FMAbabldBold",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      77.49,
      84.24,
      544.94,
      108.6
    ],
    "text": "P\u0d7a\u0d8b\u0d8d I: S\u0d7e\u0d7c. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 03.03.2025 3A",
    "fonts": [
      "MinionPro-Regular",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      125.99,
      540.95,
      165.06
    ],
    "text": "3.3 With e\ufb00 ect from the First day of July Two Thousand and Twenty Five the monthly salaries of employees will be revised and a sum of Rs.5,500/- will be added to the salary paid to such employees as at the Thirtieth day of June Two Thousand and Twenty Five.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      181.99,
      549.74,
      249.06
    ],
    "text": "4. Productivity Improvement And Elimination Of Waste.\u2013 The Employees and the Union commit their fullest co-operation to the Employer to enhance productivity levels in the factory and minimize waste in all forms in the mutual interest of preserving the future of Dipped Products PLC through the programmes conducted under the Dipped Products Productivity Improvement Schemes. In the event the business exigencies require; Employees agree to consider alternate work arrangements . The Management agrees to keep the Branch Union advised of any alternate work arrangements.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      265.99,
      549.68,
      305.06
    ],
    "text": "5. Variation of Terms And Conditions.\u2013 The Employer and the Union agree that duringthe pendency of this Agreement, they will not seek to vary, alter or add to all or any of the terms and conditions of employment presently applicable to any of the employees covered and bound by this Agreement, other than by mutual agreement.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      321.99,
      549.68,
      375.06
    ],
    "text": "6. Trade Union Action.\u2013 The Union and the Employees agree that they shall not during the pendency of this Agreement make any demands for wage increases or related allowances payments, over and above those stated in this agreement. The Union and the employees further agree that they shall not resort to any form of trade union action relating to any matter covered by this Agreement.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      387.99,
      251.03,
      399.06
    ],
    "text": "7. DISPUTE SETTLEMENT PROCEDURE.-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      9.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      85.15,
      415.99,
      549.67,
      441.06
    ],
    "text": "In the event of any industrial dispute that may arise on a matter not covered by this Agreement, parties shall endeavor to have it settled by following the dispute resolution procedure set out below:",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      97.15,
      457.99,
      549.66,
      483.06
    ],
    "text": "a) Whenever there is a dispute, a written statement of the dispute should be forwarded by the Union\u2019s branch committee to the employer, and at least two weeks given for the employer to resolve the dispute;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      97.15,
      499.99,
      549.68,
      525.06
    ],
    "text": "b) If no satisfactory solution is found, the matter should be referred to the parent union and to the Employers\u2019 Federation of Ceylon (EFC) for the purpose of attempting to resolve the dispute;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      97.15,
      541.99,
      549.67,
      567.06
    ],
    "text": "c) If after the discussion, the matter cannot be resolved by the intervention of the EFC and the parent union, conciliatory proceedings under the Industrial Disputes Act should be followed;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      97.15,
      583.99,
      549.68,
      623.06
    ],
    "text": "d) If after conciliation has failed in the Labour Department, the union wishes to take trade union action, written notice should be given of not less than 14 days to the Employer and to the EFC regarding such Trade Union action.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      99.86,
      85.96,
      487.88,
      97.48
    ],
    "text": "I fldgi: (I) fPoh \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2025'03'03",
